From c4cab3dcea15e115026ff717f29c2f9fcacbbcb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fixtures): edit and re-fit a placed mod vise pair
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SetModJaw changes a placed jaw block's figures (or slide) and regenerates
its solid through UpdateModel, as SetVise does; RefitModVise re-fits the
adjustable block to the stock as it stands (re-picks its hole and slide by
the placing fit). One undo step each, refusals by name. MCP tools
set_mod_jaw and refit_mod_vise; the jaw block row gets "Edit jaw block…"
and "Re-fit to stock".

#833 review hardening: a jaw that was not in front of the stock before a
plate edit is judged clear, so an edit that brings it 16 mm into the
stock is refused (judge_face, shared with SetModJaw); mcp_plate pins the
warning field of set_fixture_plate.

The dual-station block is held back (one stock per setup, fixtures judged
per setup - see docs/decisions/832-mod-vise-edit-refit.md).

Refs #832

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
